WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.727
Return evidence objects, not bare strings.

00:00:03.727 --> 00:00:10.632
A good evidence object includes the text, a stable source I D, perhaps a chunk I D, a score,

00:00:10.632 --> 00:00:14.606
and useful metadata such as an effective date.

00:00:15.311 --> 00:00:17.053
Why keep all of this?

00:00:17.053 --> 00:00:19.393
Because later steps need it.

00:00:19.393 --> 00:00:21.733
The grader may need the score.

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:25.753
The final answer may need the source I D for citation.

00:00:25.753 --> 00:00:28.743
Freshness checks may need an effective date.

00:00:28.743 --> 00:00:32.158
Debugging may need the exact chunk identifier.

00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:36.840
If you reduce everything to plain text too early, you lose provenance.

00:00:37.502 --> 00:00:44.449
For project work, think of every retrieved chunk as a small record, not just a sentence.

00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:49.116
Keep the metadata with the text until final validation is complete.
